## Recommended next: Batch 21c — per-tenant Xendit refactor (T2 ~18-22K, COMPLETES Direction F)

Wires up the consumer side. Refactors three call sites to read TenantXenditConfig
per-tenant instead of using shared process.env-based secrets.

Scope:
- MOD: `apps/web/src/lib/xendit.ts` — replace `getXenditClient(): Xendit` with
  `getXenditClient(tenantId: string): Promise<Xendit>`. Looks up
  TenantXenditConfig by tenantId, decrypts secretKeyEnc via @/lib/crypto, returns
  `new Xendit({secretKey})`. Throws if no config OR if isVerified=false (force
  the admin to test before customers can pay). Remove `getXenditWebhookToken()` —
  webhook token is now per-tenant and resolved by webhook handler directly.
- MOD: `apps/web/src/app/api/webhooks/xendit/route.ts` — REORDER the webhook
  handler:
    1. Read raw body + x-callback-token header
    2. Extract invoice.id from JSON payload (lightweight parse — does NOT validate sig yet)
    3. Look up EcommerceOrder.xenditPaymentId === invoice.id → get order.id + (via tenant search_path lookup or direct ctx) tenantId
    4. NOW look up TenantXenditConfig by tenantId → decrypt webhookTokenEnc
    5. timingSafeEqual(x-callback-token, decryptedToken)
    6. If match → proceed with the existing payment-status-update logic
    7. If no match → 401 (do NOT reveal whether the order exists)
  CRITICAL: tenant lookup MUST happen BEFORE signature verification because the
  token IS per-tenant. The xenditPaymentId is unauthenticated input at this
  point, but it can't be used to escalate — wrong xenditPaymentId means wrong
  tenant means wrong token means timingSafeEqual fails.
- MOD: `apps/web/src/lib/xendit-invoice.ts` — change
  `createXenditInvoiceForOrder` to accept tenantId and use the per-tenant client.
  Helper signature becomes:
  `createXenditInvoiceForOrder({tenantId, externalId, amount, description, ...})`
- MOD: `apps/web/src/server/trpc/routers/storefront.ts` — pass ctx.tenantId
  through to createXenditInvoiceForOrder in BOTH createXenditInvoice
  (protected/admin) AND placeOrderAsCustomer (public) call sites.
- MOD: `apps/web/src/__tests__/xendit-webhook.test.ts` — extend mocks:
  add tenantXenditConfig.findUnique to the @orqafy/db mock + ecommerceOrder.findFirst.
  Update existing 8 webhook tests to reflect the new per-tenant resolution order
  (mocks will need to return a TenantXenditConfig row with encrypted token).
- MOD: `apps/web/src/__tests__/storefront.test.ts` — extend mocks for the 8
  existing xendit-related tests (5 createXenditInvoice + 3 placeOrderAsCustomer
  xendit branch). All must mock tenantXenditConfig.findUnique returning a row
  with encrypted secretKeyEnc.
- NEW: `apps/web/src/__tests__/xendit-per-tenant.test.ts` — coverage of the
  new behaviors NOT already covered by extension of existing tests:
    - getXenditClient(tenantId) throws when no TenantXenditConfig row exists
    - getXenditClient(tenantId) throws when isVerified=false (force verify gate)
    - webhook handler rejects when xenditPaymentId resolves to a different
      tenant than the one whose webhook token is presented
    - webhook handler returns 401 (not 404) when xenditPaymentId doesn't
      resolve to any order (no enumeration leak)
    - cross-tenant: tenant A's webhook token cannot validate tenant B's webhook
- NO MIGRATION — TenantXenditConfig + EcommerceOrder.xenditPaymentId already exist.

Branch: feat/batch-21c-xendit-per-tenant
